# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What does Einstein's option (hidden variables) predict? {#what-does-"
"einsteins-option-hidden-variables-predict}"
msgstr ""
"아인슈타인의 선택지(숨은 변수)는 무엇을 예측하나요? {#what-does-einsteins-option-hidden-variables-"
"predict}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If Einstein's option is true, then any given pair of $e+$ and $e-$ will have"
" a set of vector components to their spins. For example, the electron might "
"have components $(+\\hat{a},-\\hat{b}, +\\hat{c})$, in which case the "
"positron must have components $(-\\hat{a},+\\hat{b}, -\\hat{c})$. We are "
"only specifying here the sign of the projection on each axis, not the "
"magnitude. Imagine we allow a very large number $N$ of such decays to take "
"place, and we collect measurements to populate the table below.\n"
msgstr ""
"아인슈타인의 선택지가 옳다면, 주어진 $e+$와 $e-$ 쌍은 각자의 스핀에 대한 벡터 성분 집합을 가집니다. 예를 들어, 전자는 성분 "
"$(+\\hat{a},-\\hat{b}, +\\hat{c})$를 가질 수 있고, 이 경우 양전자는 반드시 "
"$(-\\hat{a},+\\hat{b}, -\\hat{c})$를 가져야 합니다. 여기서는 각 축에 대한 투영의 부호만 명시할 뿐, 크기는"
" 지정하지 않습니다. 이러한 붕괴가 매우 많은 수 $N$번 일어나도록 하고, 아래 표를 채우기 위한 측정값을 수집한다고 가정해 "
"봅시다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Population  | Particle 1                                     | Particle 2                     |\n"
"|-------------|------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------|\n"
"| $N_1$       | $(+\\hat{a},+\\hat{b},+\\hat{c})$                 | $(-\\hat{a},-\\hat{b},-\\hat{c})$ |\n"
"| $N_2$       | $(+\\hat{a},+\\hat{b},-\\hat{c})$                 | $(-\\hat{a},-\\hat{b},+\\hat{c})$ |\n"
"| $N_3$       | $(+\\hat{a},-\\hat{b},+\\hat{c})$                 | $(-\\hat{a},+\\hat{b},-\\hat{c})$ |\n"
"| $N_4$       | $(+\\hat{a},-\\hat{b},-\\hat{c})$                 | $(-\\hat{a},+\\hat{b},+\\hat{c})$ |\n"
"| $N_5$       | $(-\\hat{a},+\\hat{b},+\\hat{c})$                 | $(+\\hat{a},-\\hat{b},-\\hat{c})$ |\n"
"| $N_6$       | $(-\\hat{a},+\\hat{b},-\\hat{c})$                 | $(+\\hat{a},-\\hat{b},+\\hat{c})$ |\n"
"| $N_7$       | $(-\\hat{a},-\\hat{b},+\\hat{c})$                 | $(+\\hat{a},+\\hat{b},-\\hat{c})$ |\n"
"| $N_8$       | $(-\\hat{a},-\\hat{b},-\\hat{c})$                 | $(+\\hat{a},+\\hat{b},+\\hat{c})$ |\n"
msgstr ""
"| 모집단  | 입자 1                                     | 입자 2                     |\n"
"|-------------|------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------|\n"
"| $N_1$       | $(+\\hat{a},+\\hat{b},+\\hat{c})$                 | $(-\\hat{a},-\\hat{b},-\\hat{c})$ |\n"
"| $N_2$       | $(+\\hat{a},+\\hat{b},-\\hat{c})$                 | $(-\\hat{a},-\\hat{b},+\\hat{c})$ |\n"
"| $N_3$       | $(+\\hat{a},-\\hat{b},+\\hat{c})$                 | $(-\\hat{a},+\\hat{b},-\\hat{c})$ |\n"
"| $N_4$       | $(+\\hat{a},-\\hat{b},-\\hat{c})$                 | $(-\\hat{a},+\\hat{b},+\\hat{c})$ |\n"
"| $N_5$       | $(-\\hat{a},+\\hat{b},+\\hat{c})$                 | $(+\\hat{a},-\\hat{b},-\\hat{c})$ |\n"
"| $N_6$       | $(-\\hat{a},+\\hat{b},-\\hat{c})$                 | $(+\\hat{a},-\\hat{b},+\\hat{c})$ |\n"
"| $N_7$       | $(-\\hat{a},-\\hat{b},+\\hat{c})$                 | $(+\\hat{a},+\\hat{b},-\\hat{c})$ |\n"
"| $N_8$       | $(-\\hat{a},-\\hat{b},-\\hat{c})$                 | $(+\\hat{a},+\\hat{b},+\\hat{c})$ |\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For each case in the table above, there are 9 possible choices for Lucas's "
"and Rihanna's axes: $aa$, $ab$, $ac$, $ba$, $bb$, $bc$, $ca$, $cb$, and "
"$cc$. Reading from this table, the probability of the two observers "
"measuring the same sign for rows 1 and 8 are zero. For rows 2-7, there are 4"
" ways to obtain the same sign, which we will show only for row 2:\n"
msgstr ""
"위 표의 각 경우에 대해, 루카스와 리아나가 축을 선택하는 방법은 $aa$, $ab$, $ac$, $ba$, $bb$, $bc$, "
"$ca$, $cb$, $cc$로 총 9가지입니다. 이 표를 읽으면, 1행과 8행에서 두 관측자가 같은 부호를 측정할 확률은 0임을 알 수"
" 있습니다. 2행부터 7행까지는 같은 부호를 얻을 수 있는 경우가 4가지 있으며, 이를 2행에 대해서만 살펴봐요.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Same signs: $ac$, $bc$, $ca$, $cb$\n"
"Opposite signs: $aa$, $ab$, $ba$, $bb$, $cc$\n"
msgstr ""
"같은 부호: $ac$, $bc$, $ca$, $cb$\n"
"반대 부호: $aa$, $ab$, $ba$, $bb$, $cc$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So if Einstein's option is the correct interpretation of quantum states, the total probability summed over all possible populations, of Lucas and Rihanna obtaining the same sign of spin projection on their randomly chosen axes would be:\n"
"$$ P_\\text{same}=\\frac{1}{\\sum_i{N_i}} \\frac{4}{9} (N_2+N_3+N_4+N_5+N_6+N_7)\\leq \\frac{4}{9}$$\n"
"Where equality holds only if $N_1=N_8=0$.\n"
msgstr ""
"따라서 아인슈타인의 선택지가 양자 상태에 대한 올바른 해석이라면, 모든 가능한 모집단을 합산했을 때 루카스와 리아나가 무작위로 선택한 축에서 스핀 투영의 부호가 같을 전체 확률은 다음과 같습니다.\n"
"$$ P_\\text{same}=\\frac{1}{\\sum_i{N_i}} \\frac{4}{9} (N_2+N_3+N_4+N_5+N_6+N_7)\\leq \\frac{4}{9}$$\n"
"등호는 $N_1=N_8=0$일 때만 성립합니다.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-1}"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: <Accordion>
# <AccordionItem title="정답">
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For row 2 of the chart above, we listed all the possible ways for Lucas and "
"Rihanna to obtain the same sign for their measurements, and all the ways "
"they could obtain different signs. Repeat this for the third row.\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Same signs: $ab$, $ba$, $bc$, $cb$\n"
msgstr "같은 부호: $ab$, $ba$, $bc$, $cb$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Opposite signs: $aa$, $ac$, $bb$, $ca$, $cc$\n"
msgstr "반대 부호: $aa$, $ac$, $bb$, $ca$, $cc$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The table above refers to \"populations\", meaning that we do not know how "
"many of each type of instructions nature produces, if the hidden-variables "
"treatment is correct. Show that no matter what the distribution of $N_1$ "
"through $N_8$, the probability of obtaining the same sign from measurements "
"is always less than or equal to 4/9.\n"
msgstr ""
"위 표는 \"모집단\"을 나타내며, 숨은 변수 처리가 옳다면 자연이 각 유형의 지시를 얼마나 생성하는지 알 수 없음을 의미합니다. "
"$N_1$부터 $N_8$까지의 분포가 어떠하든, 측정에서 같은 부호를 얻을 확률이 항상 4/9 이하임을 보이세요.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let us start by assuming a constant number of total measurement trials, such"
" that $\\sum_i{N_i} = N_{tot}$ is constant. Note that in the special case "
"where $N_1=N_8=0$, the expression reduces to\n"
msgstr ""
"총 측정 시행 횟수를 $\\sum_i{N_i} = N_{tot}$으로 일정하다고 가정하겠습니다. $N_1=N_8=0$인 특수한 경우, "
"식은 다음과 같이 단순화됩니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_{same}=\\frac{1}{N_2+N_3+N_4+N_5+N_6+N_7} \\times \\frac{4}{9} \\times (N_2+N_3+N_4+N_5+N_6+N_7) = \\frac{1}{N_{tot}} \\times \\frac{4}{9} \\times N_{tot}= \\frac{4}{9}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_{same}=\\frac{1}{N_2+N_3+N_4+N_5+N_6+N_7} \\times \\frac{4}{9} \\times (N_2+N_3+N_4+N_5+N_6+N_7) = \\frac{1}{N_{tot}} \\times \\frac{4}{9} \\times N_{tot}= \\frac{4}{9}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Now suppose that either $N_1 \\neq 0$ or $N_8 \\neq 0$. Then\n"
msgstr "이제 $N_1 \\neq 0$ 또는 $N_8 \\neq 0$이라고 가정해 봅시다. 그러면\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_{same}=\\frac{1}{N'_1+N'_2+N'_3+N'_4+N'_5+N'_6+N'_7+N'_8} \\times \\frac{4}{9} \\times (N'_2+N'_3+N'_4+N'_5+N'_6+N'_7) = \\frac{4}{9}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_{same}=\\frac{1}{N'_1+N'_2+N'_3+N'_4+N'_5+N'_6+N'_7+N'_8} \\times \\frac{4}{9} \\times (N'_2+N'_3+N'_4+N'_5+N'_6+N'_7) = \\frac{4}{9}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The sum of all trials, $N_tot$, is still the same as before. But since "
"$N'_1$ or $N'_8$ has increased from 0, the sum of $N'_2$ through $N'_7$ must"
" be lower than before. In particular, the sum of $N'_2$ through $N'_7$ is "
"less than $N_{tot}$. Thus\n"
msgstr ""
"전체 시행 횟수의 합 $N_tot$은 이전과 같습니다. 그러나 $N'_1$ 또는 $N'_8$이 0에서 증가했으므로, $N'_2$부터 "
"$N'_7$까지의 합은 이전보다 작아집니다. 특히, $N'_2$부터 $N'_7$까지의 합은 $N_{tot}$보다 작습니다. 따라서\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_{same}=\\frac{1}{N_{tot}} \\times \\frac{4}{9} \\times (N'_2+N'_3+N'_4+N'_5+N'_6+N'_7) < \\frac{4}{9}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_{same}=\\frac{1}{N_{tot}} \\times \\frac{4}{9} \\times (N'_2+N'_3+N'_4+N'_5+N'_6+N'_7) < \\frac{4}{9}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Combining all possible cases, we have $P_{same} \\leq \\frac{4}{9}$.\n"
msgstr "모든 가능한 경우를 종합하면, $P_{same} \\leq \\frac{4}{9}$가 성립합니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Generalization {#generalization}"
msgstr "일반화 {#generalization}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the treatment above, we considered measurements along specific axes. Of "
"course, one could make measurements along any axis. Let us call the two spin"
" vectors of two particles $\\vec{a}$ and $\\vec{b}$. Let $\\lambda$ be some "
"hidden variable such that a state of the two-particle system corresponds to "
"a well-defined value of $lambda$. Let $\\rho(\\lambda)$ be the probability "
"density in $\\lambda$.  Finally, we choose the symbols "
"$A(\\vec{a},\\lambda)$ and $B(\\vec{b},\\lambda)$ to be the pre-determined "
"outcome of a measurement performed on either particle (A or B), given the "
"spin vectors and the hidden variable. Critically, note that $A$ is "
"independent of $\\vec{b}$ and $B$ is independent of $\\vec{a}$. One could "
"now pose any number of questions related to correlations between "
"measurements on A and B. In particular, one could ask about the expectation "
"value given by\n"
msgstr ""
"앞선 처리에서는 특정 축에 따른 측정을 고려했습니다. 물론 어떤 축으로도 측정이 가능합니다. 두 입자의 스핀 벡터를 $\\vec{a}$와"
" $\\vec{b}$라고 부르겠습니다. $\\lambda$를 숨은 변수라 하면, 이 변수에 대한 특정 값이 두 입자계의 상태에 "
"대응됩니다. $\\rho(\\lambda)$를 $\\lambda$에 대한 확률 밀도라 하겠습니다. 마지막으로, "
"$A(\\vec{a},\\lambda)$와 $B(\\vec{b},\\lambda)$를 스핀 벡터와 숨은 변수가 주어졌을 때 각 입자(A "
"또는 B)에 수행된 측정의 미리 결정된 결과라고 표기합니다. 핵심적으로, $A$는 $\\vec{b}$와 독립적이고 $B$는 "
"$\\vec{a}$와 독립적임을 주목하세요. 이제 A와 B에 대한 측정 사이의 상관관계와 관련된 여러 질문을 제기할 수 있습니다. 특히,"
" 다음으로 주어지는 기댓값에 대해 질문할 수 있습니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"E(\\vec{a},\\vec{b})\\equiv\\int{d\\lambda \\rho(\\lambda)A(\\vec{a},\\lambda)B(\\vec{b},\\lambda)}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"E(\\vec{a},\\vec{b})\\equiv\\int{d\\lambda \\rho(\\lambda)A(\\vec{a},\\lambda)B(\\vec{b},\\lambda)}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given some standard assumptions on these values, like "
"$A(\\vec{a},\\lambda)\\leq 1$, $B(\\vec{b},\\lambda)\\leq 1$, and "
"normalization over $\\rho(\\lambda)$, one can show that correlations between"
" the two particles obey the relation\n"
msgstr ""
"$A(\\vec{a},\\lambda)\\leq 1$, $B(\\vec{b},\\lambda)\\leq 1$, 그리고 "
"$\\rho(\\lambda)$의 정규화와 같은 이 값들에 대한 표준적인 가정 하에서, 두 입자 간의 상관관계가 다음 관계를 따름을 보일"
" 수 있습니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|E(\\vec{a},\\vec{b})-E(\\vec{a},\\vec{d})|+|E(\\vec{c},\\vec{d})+E(\\vec{c},\\vec{b})|\\leq 2,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|E(\\vec{a},\\vec{b})-E(\\vec{a},\\vec{d})|+|E(\\vec{c},\\vec{d})+E(\\vec{c},\\vec{b})|\\leq 2,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $\\vec{a}$ and $\\vec{b}$ are the spin states of your system and "
"$\\vec{c}$ and $\\vec{d}$ are reference spin states (any other possible spin"
" states of the system). This is one of a whole class of inequalities known "
"now as \"Bell inequalities\". We won't use this general form here. Instead, "
"we will focus on one specific experimental setup, so that we can map that "
"setup onto a quantum circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"여기서 $\\vec{a}$와 $\\vec{b}$는 계의 스핀 상태이고, $\\vec{c}$와 $\\vec{d}$는 기준 스핀 상태(계의 "
"다른 가능한 스핀 상태)입니다. 이것은 현재 \"벨 부등식\"으로 알려진 일련의 부등식 중 하나입니다. 여기서는 이 일반적인 형태를 "
"사용하지 않겠습니다. 대신, 그 설정을 양자 Circuit에 매핑할 수 있도록 하나의 특정 실험 설정에 집중하겠습니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What does Born's option (non-deterministic quantum mechanics) predict? "
"{#what-does-borns-option-non-deterministic-quantum-mechanics-predict}"
msgstr ""
"Born의 선택(비결정론적 양자역학)은 무엇을 예측하나요? {#what-does-borns-option-non-deterministic-"
"quantum-mechanics-predict}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Lucas will pick some axis and find the spin of one particle to be in either the positive or negative direction. Whatever he obtains, let us orient our axes such that the $z$ axis is that direction. Then we can write the initial state after the decay of the meson and before any measurement as\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\psi \\rangle =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|+\\rangle_L|-\\rangle_R-|-\\rangle_L|+\\rangle_R)\n"
"$$\n"
"Rihanna will measure her particle's spin along some other direction at an angle $\\theta$ relative to Lucas's. The spin operator along some arbitrary direction $\\hat{n}$ is given by\n"
"$$\n"
"\\hat{S}_{\\hat{n}}=\\frac{\\hbar}{2}\\begin{bmatrix} \\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta) e^{-i\\phi} \\\\ \\sin(\\theta) e^{i\\phi} & -\\cos(\\theta) \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
"The eigenstates of this operator are\n"
"$$\n"
"|+\\rangle_{\\hat{n}}=\\cos(\\theta/2)|0\\rangle+\\sin(\\theta/2)e^{i\\phi}|1\\rangle \\\\ |-\\rangle_{\\hat{n}}=\\sin(\\theta/2)|0\\rangle-\\cos(\\theta/2)e^{i\\phi}|1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Lucas는 어떤 축을 선택해 입자 하나의 스핀이 양의 방향인지 음의 방향인지를 측정합니다. 그가 어떤 결과를 얻든, $z$ 축이 그 방향이 되도록 좌표계를 설정합시다. 그러면 중간자가 붕괴된 직후, 아무런 측정이 이루어지기 전의 초기 상태를 다음과 같이 쓸 수 있습니다.\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\psi \\rangle =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|+\\rangle_L|-\\rangle_R-|-\\rangle_L|+\\rangle_R)\n"
"$$\n"
"Rihanna는 Lucas의 축으로부터 각도 $\\theta$ 만큼 떨어진 다른 방향을 따라 자신의 입자 스핀을 측정합니다. 임의의 방향 $\\hat{n}$을 따른 스핀 연산자는 다음과 같습니다.\n"
"$$\n"
"\\hat{S}_{\\hat{n}}=\\frac{\\hbar}{2}\\begin{bmatrix} \\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta) e^{-i\\phi} \\\\ \\sin(\\theta) e^{i\\phi} & -\\cos(\\theta) \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
"이 연산자의 고유 상태는 다음과 같습니다.\n"
"$$\n"
"|+\\rangle_{\\hat{n}}=\\cos(\\theta/2)|0\\rangle+\\sin(\\theta/2)e^{i\\phi}|1\\rangle \\\\ |-\\rangle_{\\hat{n}}=\\sin(\\theta/2)|0\\rangle-\\cos(\\theta/2)e^{i\\phi}|1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-2}"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Verify that $|+\\rangle_{\\hat{n}}$ is an eigenstate of the operator "
"$\\hat{S}_{\\hat{n}}$ above, and find the eigenvalue.\n"
msgstr ""
"$|+\\rangle_{\\hat{n}}$이 위의 연산자 $\\hat{S}_{\\hat{n}}$의 고유 상태임을 검증하고, 고유값을 "
"구하세요.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{S}_{\\hat{n}}|+\\rangle_{\\hat{n}}=\\frac{\\hbar}{2}\\begin{bmatrix} \\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta) e^{-i\\phi} \\\\ \\sin(\\theta) e^{i\\phi} & -\\cos(\\theta) \\end{bmatrix} \\begin{bmatrix} \\cos(\\theta/2) \\\\ \\sin(\\theta/2)e^{i\\phi}\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"=\\frac{\\hbar}{2}\\begin{bmatrix} \\cos(\\theta)\\cos(\\theta/2) + \\sin(\\theta)\\sin(\\theta/2)e^{i\\phi} e^{-i\\phi} \\\\ \\cos(\\theta/2)\\sin(\\theta) e^{i\\phi} -\\cos(\\theta)\\sin(\\theta/2)e^{i\\phi} \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
"Using $\\cos(\\theta)=\\cos^2(\\theta/2)-\\sin^2(\\theta/2)$ and $\\sin(\\theta)=2\\cos(\\theta/2)\\sin(\\theta/2)$, we have\n"
"$$\n"
"=\\frac{\\hbar}{2}\\begin{bmatrix} \\left(\\cos(\\theta) + 2\\sin^2(\\theta/2)\\right) \\cos(\\theta/2) \\\\ \\left(2\\cos^2(\\theta/2) -\\cos^2(\\theta/2)+\\sin^2(\\theta/2)\\right)\\sin(\\theta/2)e^{i\\phi} \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"=\\frac{\\hbar}{2}\\begin{bmatrix} \\left(\\cos^2(\\theta/2)-\\sin^2(\\theta/2) + 2\\sin^2(\\theta/2)\\right) \\cos(\\theta/2) \\\\ \\left(2\\cos^2(\\theta/2) -\\cos^2(\\theta/2)+\\sin^2(\\theta/2)\\right)\\sin(\\theta/2)e^{i\\phi} \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"=\\frac{\\hbar}{2}\\begin{bmatrix} \\cos(\\theta/2) \\\\ \\sin(\\theta/2)e^{i\\phi} \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
"This demonstrates that $|+\\rangle_{\\hat{n}}$ is an eigenstate and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\frac{\\hbar}{2}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{S}_{\\hat{n}}|+\\rangle_{\\hat{n}}=\\frac{\\hbar}{2}\\begin{bmatrix} \\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta) e^{-i\\phi} \\\\ \\sin(\\theta) e^{i\\phi} & -\\cos(\\theta) \\end{bmatrix} \\begin{bmatrix} \\cos(\\theta/2) \\\\ \\sin(\\theta/2)e^{i\\phi}\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"=\\frac{\\hbar}{2}\\begin{bmatrix} \\cos(\\theta)\\cos(\\theta/2) + \\sin(\\theta)\\sin(\\theta/2)e^{i\\phi} e^{-i\\phi} \\\\ \\cos(\\theta/2)\\sin(\\theta) e^{i\\phi} -\\cos(\\theta)\\sin(\\theta/2)e^{i\\phi} \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
"$\\cos(\\theta)=\\cos^2(\\theta/2)-\\sin^2(\\theta/2)$와 $\\sin(\\theta)=2\\cos(\\theta/2)\\sin(\\theta/2)$를 이용하면,\n"
"$$\n"
"=\\frac{\\hbar}{2}\\begin{bmatrix} \\left(\\cos(\\theta) + 2\\sin^2(\\theta/2)\\right) \\cos(\\theta/2) \\\\ \\left(2\\cos^2(\\theta/2) -\\cos^2(\\theta/2)+\\sin^2(\\theta/2)\\right)\\sin(\\theta/2)e^{i\\phi} \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"=\\frac{\\hbar}{2}\\begin{bmatrix} \\left(\\cos^2(\\theta/2)-\\sin^2(\\theta/2) + 2\\sin^2(\\theta/2)\\right) \\cos(\\theta/2) \\\\ \\left(2\\cos^2(\\theta/2) -\\cos^2(\\theta/2)+\\sin^2(\\theta/2)\\right)\\sin(\\theta/2)e^{i\\phi} \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"=\\frac{\\hbar}{2}\\begin{bmatrix} \\cos(\\theta/2) \\\\ \\sin(\\theta/2)e^{i\\phi} \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
"이로써 $|+\\rangle_{\\hat{n}}$이 고유 상태이고 해당 고유값이 $\\frac{\\hbar}{2}$임이 증명됩니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The probability of Lucas measuring a spin to be in the positive direction along the axis he chose $|+\\rangle$ $and$ that Rihanna also measures a positive spin along her chosen direction $|+\\rangle_{\\hat{n}}$ is\n"
"$$\n"
"P_{++}=\\left|\\left(_L\\langle+|_{R,\\hat{n}}\\langle+|\\right)|\\psi\\rangle\\right|^2\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"P_{++}=\\left|  \\left(_L\\langle+|_R\\left(\\cos(\\theta/2)\\langle+|+\\sin(\\theta/2)e^{-i\\phi}\\langle-|\\right)\\right)  \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(|+\\rangle_L|-\\rangle_R-|-\\rangle_L|+\\rangle_R\\right)    \\right|^2\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"P_{++}=\\frac{1}{2}\\left|  \\left(_L\\langle+|_R\\left(\\cos(\\theta/2)\\langle+|+\\sin(\\theta/2)e^{-i\\phi}\\langle-|\\right)\\right)  \\left(|+\\rangle_L|-\\rangle_R\\right)    \\right|^2\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"P_{++}=\\frac{1}{2}\\left|  \\left(\\sin(\\theta/2)e^{-i\\phi}\\vphantom{p}_R\\langle-|\\right) |-\\rangle_R    \\right|^2\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"P_{++}=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin^2(\\theta/2)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Lucas가 자신의 선택한 축 방향으로 스핀을 양의 방향 $|+\\rangle$으로 측정하고, Rihanna 역시 자신의 선택한 방향으로 양의 스핀 $|+\\rangle_{\\hat{n}}$을 측정할 확률은 다음과 같습니다.\n"
"$$\n"
"P_{++}=\\left|\\left(_L\\langle+|_{R,\\hat{n}}\\langle+|\\right)|\\psi\\rangle\\right|^2\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"P_{++}=\\left|  \\left(_L\\langle+|_R\\left(\\cos(\\theta/2)\\langle+|+\\sin(\\theta/2)e^{-i\\phi}\\langle-|\\right)\\right)  \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(|+\\rangle_L|-\\rangle_R-|-\\rangle_L|+\\rangle_R\\right)    \\right|^2\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"P_{++}=\\frac{1}{2}\\left|  \\left(_L\\langle+|_R\\left(\\cos(\\theta/2)\\langle+|+\\sin(\\theta/2)e^{-i\\phi}\\langle-|\\right)\\right)  \\left(|+\\rangle_L|-\\rangle_R\\right)    \\right|^2\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"P_{++}=\\frac{1}{2}\\left|  \\left(\\sin(\\theta/2)e^{-i\\phi}\\vphantom{p}_R\\langle-|\\right) |-\\rangle_R    \\right|^2\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"P_{++}=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin^2(\\theta/2)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-3}"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Do the same for $P_{--}$. Verify that it also equals "
"$\\frac{1}{2}\\sin^2(\\theta).$\n"
msgstr "$P_{--}$에 대해서도 같은 계산을 수행하세요. 이 값 역시 $\\frac{1}{2}\\sin^2(\\theta)$임을 검증하세요.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_{--}=\\left|\\left(_L\\langle-|_{R,\\hat{-n}}\\langle+|\\right)|\\psi\\rangle\\right|^2\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"P_{--}=\\left|  \\left(_L\\langle-|_R\\left(\\sin(\\theta/2)\\langle+|-\\cos(\\theta/2)e^{-i\\phi}\\langle-|\\right)\\right)  \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(|+\\rangle_L|-\\rangle_R-|-\\rangle_L|+\\rangle_R\\right)    \\right|^2\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"P_{--}=\\frac{1}{2}\\left|  \\left(_L\\langle-|_R\\left(\\sin(\\theta/2)\\langle+|-\\cos(\\theta/2)e^{-i\\phi}\\langle-|\\right)\\right)  \\left(-|-\\rangle_L|+\\rangle_R\\right)    \\right|^2\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"P_{--}=\\frac{1}{2}\\left|  \\left(\\sin(\\theta/2) \\vphantom{p}_R\\langle+|\\right) |+\\rangle_R    \\right|^2\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"P_{--}=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin^2(\\theta/2)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_{--}=\\left|\\left(_L\\langle-|_{R,\\hat{-n}}\\langle+|\\right)|\\psi\\rangle\\right|^2\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"P_{--}=\\left|  \\left(_L\\langle-|_R\\left(\\sin(\\theta/2)\\langle+|-\\cos(\\theta/2)e^{-i\\phi}\\langle-|\\right)\\right)  \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(|+\\rangle_L|-\\rangle_R-|-\\rangle_L|+\\rangle_R\\right)    \\right|^2\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"P_{--}=\\frac{1}{2}\\left|  \\left(_L\\langle-|_R\\left(\\sin(\\theta/2)\\langle+|-\\cos(\\theta/2)e^{-i\\phi}\\langle-|\\right)\\right)  \\left(-|-\\rangle_L|+\\rangle_R\\right)    \\right|^2\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"P_{--}=\\frac{1}{2}\\left|  \\left(\\sin(\\theta/2) \\vphantom{p}_R\\langle+|\\right) |+\\rangle_R    \\right|^2\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"P_{--}=\\frac{1}{2}\\sin^2(\\theta/2)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Adding these results, we find that the probability of the signs of the two "
"measured axes are the same $P_{\\text{same}}=\\sin^2(\\theta/2)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"이 두 결과를 더하면, 두 측정축에서 부호가 같을 확률은 $P_{\\text{same}}=\\sin^2(\\theta/2)$임을 알 수 "
"있습니다.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-4}"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What could you do to check the math of this result? To be clear, we're not "
"asking you to verify yet that it matches nature, just to make sure nothing "
"went wrong in all the math.\n"
msgstr ""
"이 결과의 수학적 검증을 위해 어떤 방법을 사용할 수 있을까요? 여기서는 자연과의 일치를 확인하는 것이 아니라, 계산 과정에서 오류가 "
"없는지를 확인하는 것입니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '(1) '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Do the same calculation for $P_{\\text{diff}}=\\cos^2(\\theta/2)$ to verify "
"the conservation of probability.\n"
msgstr "$P_{\\text{diff}}=\\cos^2(\\theta/2)$에 대해 같은 계산을 수행하여 확률 보존을 검증하세요.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '(2) '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Check a known case. Insert $\\theta = 0$. Then $P_{\\text{same}}$ "
"corresponds to the two observers each measuring their spin along the same "
"axis, which would violate conservation of angular momentum. So you would "
"expect that probability to be zero, and indeed inserting $\\theta = 0$ "
"yields $\\sin^2(0/2) = 0$.\n"
msgstr ""
"알려진 경우를 확인하세요. $\\theta = 0$을 대입합니다. 이 경우 $P_{\\text{same}}$은 두 관측자가 동일한 축을 "
"따라 스핀을 측정하는 경우에 해당하는데, 이는 각운동량 보존 법칙에 위배됩니다. 따라서 그 확률이 0이어야 하고, 실제로 $\\theta"
" = 0$을 대입하면 $\\sin^2(0/2) = 0$이 됩니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '(3) '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Check a different known case. Try $\\theta = \\pi$. What should you obtain. "
"Careful of that $\\frac{1}{2}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"또 다른 알려진 경우를 확인하세요. $\\theta = \\pi$를 대입해 보세요. 어떤 결과가 나와야 할지 생각해 보세요. "
"$\\frac{1}{2}$에 주의하세요.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We were specifically sketching the case where axes are at $120\\deg$ "
"relative to each other. Remember, whatever direction ($\\pm a$, $\\pm b$, or"
" $\\pm c$) Lucas obtains, we call that $z$. Then Rihanna randomly chooses to"
" measure along either $\\pm a$, $\\pm b$, or $\\pm c$. If her choice is the "
"same as Lucas's (up to a sign), then they are both measuring along $z$, and "
"the probability of Rihanna also measuring $+z$ is zero. This should happen "
"1/3 of the time, since Rihanna's choice of axis is independent of Lucas's "
"choice. For any other choice, Rihanna will be measuring along an axis either"
" $120\\deg = 2\\pi/3$ radians from $z$ (1/3 of the time) or $240\\deg = "
"4\\pi/3$ radians from $z$ (1/3 of the time). And of course, along either of "
"those axes, the spin could be measured to be in the positive or negative "
"direction. This gives us a total probability of Lucas and Rihanna obtaining "
"the same sign:\n"
msgstr ""
"우리는 구체적으로 세 축이 서로 $120\\deg$ 간격으로 배치된 경우를 살펴보고 있습니다. Lucas가 어떤 방향($\\pm a$, "
"$\\pm b$, 또는 $\\pm c$)을 측정하든, 그 방향을 $z$라고 부르겠습니다. 그러면 Rihanna는 $\\pm a$, "
"$\\pm b$, 또는 $\\pm c$ 중 하나를 무작위로 선택해 측정합니다. Rihanna의 선택이 Lucas의 선택과 같은 "
"축이라면(부호는 달라도 무방합니다), 두 사람 모두 $z$를 측정하는 것이므로 Rihanna가 $+z$를 측정할 확률은 0입니다. 이는 "
"Rihanna의 축 선택이 Lucas의 선택과 독립적이기 때문에, 전체 경우의 1/3에 해당합니다. 그 외의 경우, Rihanna는 "
"$z$로부터 $120\\deg = 2\\pi/3$ 라디안 떨어진 축(전체의 1/3)이나, $240\\deg = 4\\pi/3$ 라디안 "
"떨어진 축(전체의 1/3)을 측정하게 됩니다. 물론 각 축에서 스핀은 양 또는 음의 방향으로 측정될 수 있습니다. 이를 통해 Lucas와"
" Rihanna가 같은 부호를 얻을 전체 확률을 구할 수 있습니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_{\\text{same}} = \\frac{1}{3}\\left(   0 + \\sin^2(\\pi/3) + \\sin^2(2\\pi/3)     \\right) = \\frac{1}{3}\\left(   0 + \\frac{3}{4} + \\frac{3}{4}     \\right) = \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_{\\text{same}} = \\frac{1}{3}\\left(   0 + \\sin^2(\\pi/3) + \\sin^2(2\\pi/3)     \\right) = \\frac{1}{3}\\left(   0 + \\frac{3}{4} + \\frac{3}{4}     \\right) = \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Wow {#wow}"
msgstr "놀랍습니다 {#wow}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We just showed that\n"
msgstr "방금 우리는 다음을 보였습니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(P_\\text{same})_\\text{max, Einstein}<(P_\\text{same})_\\text{max, Born}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(P_\\text{same})_\\text{max, Einstein}<(P_\\text{same})_\\text{max, Born}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Let's take a step back.\n"
msgstr "잠시 멈추고 생각해 봅시다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Einstein's and Born's options seemed like they would always yield the same "
"results, since they only differed in their description of what happens prior"
" to measurement. And yet, assuming there were instructions that pre-"
"determined the sign of the spin measurement along certain axes, we obtained "
"a constraint on the probability for the measurements to yield the same sign "
"$(P_{\\text{same}})_\\text{Einstein}\\leq\\frac{4}{9}$. Then we assumed "
"probability distributions as in quantum mechanics... and obtained a "
"different value for $(P_{\\text{same}})_\\text{Born}=\\frac{1}{2}$. The "
"prediction from quantum mechanics is higher than that allowed by the hidden "
"variables treatment. So we can actually do an experiment and discover "
"whether quantum mechanical states are determined by nature prior to "
"measurement, or if they are truly in a probabilistic superposition of "
"possible states.\n"
msgstr ""
"아인슈타인의 선택과 Born의 선택은 측정 이전에 일어나는 일에 대한 설명만 다를 뿐, 항상 같은 결과를 낼 것처럼 보였습니다. 그런데 "
"스핀 측정의 부호를 특정 축에 따라 미리 결정하는 숨은 변수가 있다고 가정했을 때, 같은 부호를 측정할 확률에 대한 제약 "
"$(P_{\\text{same}})_\\text{Einstein}\\leq\\frac{4}{9}$이 도출되었습니다. 반면, 양자역학에서와"
" 같은 확률 분포를 가정했을 때는 다른 값 $(P_{\\text{same}})_\\text{Born}=\\frac{1}{2}$가 "
"얻어졌습니다. 양자역학의 예측값이 숨은 변수 이론이 허용하는 범위보다 더 큽니다. 따라서 실험을 통해 양자역학적 상태가 측정 이전에 "
"자연에 의해 결정되어 있는지, 아니면 진정한 확률론적 중첩 상태에 있는지를 실제로 알아낼 수 있습니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This experiment has been done many times using many different physical "
"systems, often photons. There are many subtle considerations, such as biases"
" in measurement, the timing(simultaneity) of measurements, and many others. "
"Over the decades, concerns about these subtleties have been steadily eroded."
" Tests are still implemented, as we learn more about reality, but there is "
"now broad agreement that the answer you'll obtain here, using IBM&reg; "
"quantum computers, is correct.\n"
msgstr ""
"이 실험은 주로 광자를 이용한 다양한 물리계에서 수차례 수행되었습니다. 측정에서의 편향, 측정의 타이밍(동시성), 그리고 그 외 여러 "
"미묘한 사항들이 고려되어야 합니다. 수십 년에 걸쳐 이러한 미묘한 문제들에 대한 우려는 꾸준히 해소되어 왔습니다. 현실에 대해 더 많이 "
"알아감에 따라 여전히 실험이 계속 이루어지고 있지만, 지금은 여기서 IBM&reg; 양자 컴퓨터를 사용해 얻게 될 결과가 옳다는 광범위한"
" 합의가 이루어져 있습니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Test using real quantum computers! {#test-using-real-quantum-computers}"
msgstr "실제 양자 컴퓨터로 테스트해 보세요! {#test-using-real-quantum-computers}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In keeping with our treatment above, let us define the direction of Lucas's measurement to be $+z$. This was convenient even in the algebraic approach, but it is especially convenient for quantum computation, since what is typically measured is the qubit's projection along $z$.\n"
"We want to make a quantum circuit that gives us the same probability conditions as those above for $P_{++}$. We are free to orient our plane such that $\\phi=0$, and we obtain\n"
"$$\n"
"P_{++}=\\left|  \\left(_L\\langle+|_R\\left(\\cos(\\theta/2)\\langle+|+\\sin(\\theta/2)\\langle-|\\right)\\right)  \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(|+\\rangle_L|-\\rangle_R-|-\\rangle_L|+\\rangle_R\\right)    \\right|^2\n"
"$$\n"
"We need to know a few things about IBM quantum computers, to guide our discussion. Firstly, qubits start out initialized in the $|0\\rangle = |+\\rangle_z$ state. As mentioned, before, when measurements are made, they are along the $z$ axis. So the goal is to determine what operators we can insert between the measurement basis states $\\langle 0|\\langle 0|$ and the initial states of the qubits $|0\\rangle |0\\rangle$ to obtain the complicated expression above. For that, we'll need to review some basic gates in quantum computing.\n"
msgstr ""
"위에서 다룬 방식에 따라, Lucas의 측정 방향을 $+z$로 정의하겠습니다. 이는 대수적 접근법에서도 편리했지만, 양자 컴퓨팅에서는 특히 유용합니다. 일반적으로 Qubit의 $z$ 방향 투영이 측정되기 때문입니다.\n"
"우리는 위에서 $P_{++}$에 대해 구한 확률 조건과 동일한 확률을 가지는 양자 Circuit을 만들고 싶습니다. 평면을 $\\phi=0$이 되도록 설정하면 다음을 얻습니다.\n"
"$$\n"
"P_{++}=\\left|  \\left(_L\\langle+|_R\\left(\\cos(\\theta/2)\\langle+|+\\sin(\\theta/2)\\langle-|\\right)\\right)  \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(|+\\rangle_L|-\\rangle_R-|-\\rangle_L|+\\rangle_R\\right)    \\right|^2\n"
"$$\n"
"논의를 이어가기 위해 IBM 양자 컴퓨터에 대해 몇 가지 알아야 할 사항이 있습니다. 먼저, Qubit은 $|0\\rangle = |+\\rangle_z$ 상태로 초기화됩니다. 앞서 언급했듯이, 측정은 $z$ 축을 따라 이루어집니다. 따라서 목표는 측정 기저 상태 $\\langle 0|\\langle 0|$와 Qubit의 초기 상태 $|0\\rangle |0\\rangle$ 사이에 어떤 연산자를 삽입해야 위의 복잡한 식을 얻을 수 있는지 알아내는 것입니다. 이를 위해 양자 컴퓨팅의 기본 Gate를 복습해야 합니다.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$X$ gate: Equivalent to a NOT operation. Single-qubit gate.\n"
"$$\n"
"X|0\\rangle = |1\\rangle,\\\\X|1\\rangle=|0\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"X=\\begin{bmatrix} 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$X$ Gate: NOT 연산에 해당합니다. 단일 qubit Gate입니다.\n"
"$$\n"
"X|0\\rangle = |1\\rangle,\\\\X|1\\rangle=|0\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"X=\\begin{bmatrix} 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In Qiskit, creating a circuit with an $X$ gate looks like this:\n"
msgstr "Qiskit에서 $X$ Gate가 포함된 Circuit을 만들면 다음과 같습니다.\n"

